= Conclusion

The paired experiment provides the linear KF baseline and comparison curves required by the project while varying bearing and range noise independently at a fixed process covariance. Nonlinear filters reduce the baseline's velocity error in the tested conditions, but position rankings depend on the noise component and level. CKF and SCKF give the same displayed accuracy, while SCKF incurs higher measured runtime. The next revision should strengthen model-controlled comparisons and uncertainty assessment before making broader claims about filter superiority.
